    "sha256": "17d8316f065926505d21fb773ae5d9b76883c567ee9451cb8dafb1f8080175ba",
    "selection_code": "tbl = pq.read_table(f\"{DATA}/{args.which}_rl.parquet\")\nprompt_msgs = tbl[\"prompt\"][0].as_py()\nPERMILLE = val_doc_permille(50000, len(tbl))\ndocs, seen = [], set()\nfor i in range(len(tbl)):\n    uid = tbl[\"doc_id\"][i].as_py()\n    if uid in seen or not is_val_doc(uid, PERMILLE) or uid not in meta: continue\n    seen.add(uid)\n    docs.append((uid, np.array(tbl[\"activation_vector\"][i].as_py(), dtype=np.float32)))\n    if len(docs) >= args.n: break\nprint(f\"{args.which}: scanning {len(docs)} held-out problems\", flush=True)\n\n"
  },
  "explanation": "The historical score scan independently selected the first 60 unique document-hash-held-out problems from each reader's own activation parquet. The parquets and their lengths differed, and the validation hash fraction was computed from each length. Consequently h24 and z have different question sets. Each current lens reference uses exactly its corresponding reader's original questions. AO used a separate 48-question evaluation set.",
  "comparison_limit": "Historical h24 versus z reader curves are not a paired question comparison. The 12-question overlap can be replotted from saved descriptions; a larger common-set historical scan needs new reader inference."
